tags: event

= Wendan Conference

At the Wendan Conference, the western realms met with Commonwealth representatives to resolve the issue of War Loans once and for all. Given the ongoing economic crisis, they concluded that the Commonwealth would be unable to resume payments after the moratorium ends.

Therefore, our War Loans have been reduced by 90%! In the end, the Commonwealth is required to make only a final payment of three billion crowns, effectively ending future War Loan obligations. This has greatly boosted investor confidence and sparked a new wave of capital inflows to the Commonwealth. This should reduce the strain on our budget. [? if marcher_in_government and foreign_minister_party == "Marcher": Even though this is not our accomplishment, our foreign ministry is eager to take credit for it. ?][? if not marcher_in_government and foreign_minister_party != "Marcher": Even though this is not the work of the foreign ministry, it is eager to take credit for it. ?]

[? if bruning_time: Askew, having skillfully leveraged the issues of foreign policy and War Loans, stands to gain significantly. He has long argued that his austerity and deflationary measures were justified if they led to the abolition of War Loans—and now, that vision has been realized. President DuFour is ecstatic at this outcome, lauding Askew’s diplomatic prowess alongside his inner circle. Meanwhile, the urgency to bring the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span> into government has waned, with many believing their support has reached their peak. ?]

- @military_parity
- @military_parity_bruning

@military_parity
title: But of course, Staal stipulates that we demand military parity.
subtitle: This will be a severe betrayal of our values!
view-if: staal_marcher and president == "DuFour" and foreign_minister_party == "Marcher"
on-arrival: military_parity = 1 if eu or (west_relation >= 6 and reformist_strength >= left_strength + center_strength and soviet_relation == 0 and collectivist_relation < 30); army_strength += 300 if military_parity; warden_strength -= 100 if military_parity; loyalist_strength -= 50 if military_parity; banner_strength -= 150 if military_parity; army_militancy += 2 if military_parity; commons_marcher -= 6; guild_marcher -= 2; burgher_marcher -= 4; landed_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; disfavored_marcher -= 4; commons_collectivist += 6; guild_ddp += 2; burgher_ddp += 4; landed_ddp += 2; faithful_collectivist += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 4; guild_marcher += 20 if military_parity; commons_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; disfavored_royalist -= 4 if military_parity; burgher_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; guild_royalist -= 15 if military_parity; landed_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; faithful_royalist -= 3 if military_parity; left_dissent += 50; center_dissent += 40; labor_dissent += 30; reformist_dissent += 20; knight_dissent += 20; left_strength -= 20; center_strength -= 10; ddp_relation -= 5; gold_relation += 15; gold_left += 5; ddp_left += 10; ddp_cohesion += 5; lvp_relation += 5; burgher_ddp += 10 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; burgher_marcher -= 10 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; commons_ddp += 5 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; commons_marcher -= 5 if ddp_leader == "Thayer"; west_relation -= 3; eu_progress -= 2

General Staal has demanded that we raise the issue of rearmament, which remains restricted under the Treaty of Etaluxia. However, the new <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> sovereign, [? if left_cartel_france: Edwyn Validar II ?][? if not left_cartel_france: Martyn Validar II ?], seized on this as an admission that the Commonwealth is, in fact, capable of paying its War Loans and would simply redirect freed-up funds toward rearmament.

[? if military_parity:[? if eu: However, with the formation of the <span style="color: #FFDD00;">Regional Concordant</span> and its defense agreements, preventing the Commonwealth’s rearmament has become increasingly irrelevant. As a result, military restrictions are lifted!?][? if not eu: However, our exceptionally friendly relations with the <span style="color: #0A3161;">Western</span> <span style="color: #C8102E;">realms</span> have led them to begrudgingly grant us flexibility in rearmament, believing that we could serve as a bulwark against the <span style="color: #700000;">revolutionaries</span>.?] As a result, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> has lost yet another propaganda tool. However, we continue to suffer heavy losses to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, who we have suffered serious defections to?]. ?]

[? if not military_parity: This has caused great embarrassment to our pacifist and democratic image, both at home and abroad. Staal has played us false! ?]

@military_parity_bruning
title: [? if not concord_formed: But of course, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, in Askew's coalition demands the right to rearm. ?][? if concord_formed: But of course, the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> in the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> demands the right to rearm. ?]
