on-arrival: west_relation -= 2; eu_progress -= 1; bruning_coalition_dissent += 2; traditionalist_angry += 3; guild_traditionalist -= 5; guild_dnf += 3; guild_royalist += 3; landed_traditionalist -= 3; landed_dnf += 3; commons_traditionalist -= 2; commons_royalist += 2; disfavored_traditionalist -= 2; disfavored_royalist += 2; faithful_traditionalist -= 2; faithful_royalist += 2

General Staal, [? if president == "DuFour": the [? if not concord_formed: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if concord_formed: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span>?], and President DuFour?][? if president != "DuFour": and the [? if not concord_formed: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if concord_formed: <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span>?]?] have pressured Askew to raise the issue of rearmament, which remains restricted under the Treaty of Etaluxia, and the hated National-Debt Clause. However, the new <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> sovereign, [? if left_cartel_france: Edwyn Validar II ?][? if not left_cartel_france: Martyn Validar II ?], seized on this as an admission that the Commonwealth is indeed capable of paying War Loans and would simply redirect any freed-up funds toward rearmament.

Already wary of the right-wing elements in Askew’s cabinet, the <span style="color: #002654;">Ethian</span> have good reason to reject these demands. The controversy has only increased tensions within Askew’s government.    

